description:
Lines 294, 691, 961, 1044: The code consistently uses saturating_add for size calculations and explicit bounds checks before u16 casts. This prevents integer overflow vulnerabilities in size calculations.

Example (line 691-695):
```rust
let total_udp = 8usize.saturating_add(coap_len);
if total_udp > u16::MAX as usize {
    return Err(BufferTooSmall::new(total_udp, u16::MAX as usize).into());
}
let udp_len = total_udp as u16;
```

This pattern is correct and worth preserving.
